    "turn_idx": 90,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. It's true. Pittsburgh, we produce more steel than the rest of the country combined in World War II. And there were steel mills all up and down the rivers. Youngston, Ohio, and then China started to subsidize their steel and they dumped steel in the United States and pretty soon we couldn't afford it anymore. You know, we couldn't compete with them.",
